Every diagonal element of the stated Cartan subalgebra has the form
$$
\operatorname{diag}(0,t_1,t_2,-t_1,-t_2).
$$
Let $\varepsilon_i$ extract $t_i$. The roots are the <B2 root system>
$$
\boxed{\Phi=\{\pm\varepsilon_1,\pm\varepsilon_2,
\pm\varepsilon_1\pm\varepsilon_2\}}.
$$

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= b
{parent=3}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Choose
$$
\boxed{\alpha_1=\varepsilon_1-\varepsilon_2,\qquad
\alpha_2=\varepsilon_2}.
$$
Here $\alpha_1$ is long and $\alpha_2$ is short. The <Dynkin diagram> consists of two vertices joined by a double edge, with its arrow pointing from $\alpha_1$ toward the shorter root $\alpha_2$:
$$
\alpha_1\Longrightarrow\alpha_2.
$$

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= c
{parent=3}
