The <classification of finite-dimensional sl2 representations> says that for every $n\geq0$ there is one irreducible module $V(n)$ of dimension $n+1$, with weights
$$
n,n-2,\ldots,-n
$$
of multiplicity one, and every finite-dimensional $\mathfrak{sl}_2(\mathbb C)$-module is a direct sum of these irreducibles.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

